-- `X` holds an `F(X)`: positive while `F` is, and accepted then, the store filing the verdict by `X`'s identity with what it read of `F`, digested with no vector. Stepped to again once `F` is negative, it is looked for among those records first.
induct /app/X: pub Type
| c(n: #{node = InductType, universes = {levels = [0]}} /lib/F(#{node = InductType} /app/X()))
end
